WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:18.551
In an instant Roxy changed into Rocket Girl.

2
00:00:18.552 --> 00:00:22.304
"It's time to find that art thief!" said Roxy.

3
00:00:22.305 --> 00:00:28.170
She blasted up into the sky.

4
00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:33.135
When Roxy arrived at the Metro City Art Gallery, she laughed.

5
00:00:33.136 --> 00:00:36.359
Detective Smith was crawling around on the floor.

6
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.011
"Uh, Detective," Roxy asked with a grin.

7
00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:44.620
"Aren't you a little old to be playing on the floor?"

8
00:00:44.621 --> 00:00:47.875
Detective Smith frowned as he stood up.

9
00:00:47.876 --> 00:00:51.468
"I wasn't playing on the floor," he said.

10
00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:53.556
"I was looking at this."

11
00:00:53.557 --> 00:00:57.281
Detective Smith held up a ball about the size of a baseball.

12
00:00:57.282 --> 00:01:00.046
It had a small lightning bolt on one side.

13
00:01:00.047 --> 00:01:02.987
On the other side was the word "fog."

14
00:01:02.988 --> 00:01:07.987
"Aha!" said Roxy. "That ball belongs to Weatherman!"

15
00:01:07.988 --> 00:01:11.344
"You're right!" said Detective Smith.

16
00:01:11.345 --> 00:01:17.420
"He uses Weather Balls to create bad weather.

17
00:01:17.421 --> 00:01:19.271
I talked to a witness.

18
00:01:19.272 --> 00:01:23.839
She said the art gallery was filled with fog during the robbery."

19
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.473
"Hmm," said Roxy.

20
00:01:26.474 --> 00:01:29.863
"So no one could see who was stealing the paintings."

21
00:01:29.864 --> 00:01:32.882
"Exactly!" said Detective Smith.

22
00:01:32.883 --> 00:01:35.236
Just then his phone rang.

23
00:01:35.237 --> 00:01:41.015
"Hello?" he said. "Good! Don't lose him!"

24
00:01:41.016 --> 00:01:44.262
Detective Smith hung up his phone and looked at Roxy.

25
00:01:44.263 --> 00:01:47.734
"Police found Weatherman driving down West Street.

26
00:01:47.735 --> 00:01:49.949
They're chasing him now."

27
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:54.577
Without saying a word, Roxy flew out of the gallery.

28
00:01:54.578 --> 00:01:58.383
On West Street three police cars were chasing a black van.

29
00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:07.299
Two lightning bolts were painted on the van's sides.

30
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.406
Suddenly a thick fog filled the street.

31
00:02:11.407 --> 00:02:15.785
The police lost sight of the van, which darted down an alley.

32
00:02:15.786 --> 00:02:18.592
"More fog, huh?" said Roxy.

33
00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:22.008
"That's not a problem for Rocket Girl!"

34
00:02:22.009 --> 00:02:25.529
Roxy took a deep breath and blew as hard as she could.

35
00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.687
The fog cleared instantly.

36
00:02:27.688 --> 00:02:31.470
Now Roxy could see Weatherman's van a few blocks away.

37
00:02:31.471 --> 00:02:34.957
She flew after it.

38
00:02:34.958 --> 00:02:36.484
Whiz-hoo!

39
00:02:36.485 --> 00:02:42.097
Roxy fired her eye laser beams, burning a hole in the back of the van.

40
00:02:42.098 --> 00:02:46.878
The van skidded to a stop, and Weatherman jumped out.

41
00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:51.135
"You ruined the Weather Van!" he yelled.

42
00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:55.805
"You're going to pay for that, Rocket Girl!"

43
00:02:55.806 --> 00:03:00.411
Weatherman grabbed a Weather Ball from the back of the van.

44
00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:02.383
He threw it into the air.

45
00:03:02.384 --> 00:03:09.633
"Weather Ball, activate!"

46
00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:13.820
The whole sky grew dark. Clouds moved in.

47
00:03:13.821 --> 00:03:15.766
And then—crack!

48
00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:18.888
A giant lightning bolt shot down from the sky.

49
00:03:18.889 --> 00:03:24.320
And it was headed straight toward Roxy!
